1
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:02,340
targets I'm waiting
for you to wait for you

2
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:12,417
I'm going to burn my heart
I'm going to die the next day

3
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:17,180
I'm going to die the next day
I'm going to die the next day

4
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:34,457
We all returned to the digital world so
we could rebuild the primary village,

5
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:36,837
which was damaged during
our battles with Ken.

6
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:40,297
It was hard work, but we had fun
playing with the baby Punimon.

7
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:42,262
While Digmon and I were working,

8
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:43,777
we were attacked by Thundermon,

9
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:47,397
And for the first time, Armadyllamon
digifogged to Aquilamon.

10
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,557
He couldn't defeat Thundermon on his own,

11
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:53,897
but suddenly Stingmon appeared and saved
me while helping to destroy Thundermon.

12
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:55,337
I didn't know who he was,

13
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:57,417
but it became clear when Ken showed up and

14
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,520
Stingmon returned to a
form we all recognized.

15
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:01,950
Wormmon.

16
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:12,177
I think Kari's total babe, dude.

17
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:15,740
What's with Davis and his
goggles? Lunchroom duty. Yuck.

18
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,317
I know what you mean.

19
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,257
These outfits are totally humiliating.

20
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:20,220
You said it.

21
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:22,977
We look like a couple of
salt and pepper shakers.

22
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,520
Or mad scientists. Ew. Yuck.

23
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:28,557
You know, maybe Ken isn't
such a bad guy after all.

24
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:29,560
I'm not sure.

25
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:31,173
He helped us last time.

26
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:32,460
I don't know.

27
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:33,977
He'll have to prove it to me.

28
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:35,657
He's done some evil things in the past.

29
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:37,740
Hey, man, I want my lunch already.

30
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,257
Technically, Ken is one
of the Digidestined.

31
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,869
I was thinking of asking
him to join our...

32
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:47,940
I guess that's a no from Cody. I
don't know. It was just an idea.

33
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,485
I thought maybe he could help.

34
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:54,278
I guess someone hasn't had
their coffee this morning.

35
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:56,720
Ken, one of us? Impossible.

36
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:59,577
When he was the Digimon
Emperor, he was ruthless.

37
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:01,557
He might be pulling another trick on us.

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,877
I think Ken's changed.

39
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,937
He's not the Digimon Emperor anymore.

40
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,060
I don't know.

41
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:07,340
What do you mean?

42
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,357
I thought Ken changed too,
especially after Wormon got hurt.

43
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,297
it seemed like he finally
realized that Digimon

44
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:14,117
were living creatures that have feelings.

45
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:17,057
But after our last battle in the
digital world, I'm not so sure.

46
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,787
He seemed a whole lot
like the old kin to me.

47
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:24,557
The way he mercilessly ordered
Stingmon to go in for the kill.

48
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:25,880
The poor Digimon.

49
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:27,920
It was just horrible.

50
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:32,117
I'm sorry, Davis, but I don't think I
can trust him, not after what he did.

51
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,660
No one ever believes me.

52
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,958
I'll just have to do this on my own.

53
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:37,340
Davis, wait for me.

54
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:39,160
Hey, Davis, what's up?

55
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:40,630
Where are they going?

56
00:03:40,713 --> 00:03:43,597
I don't know, but I think he's mad
at me for disagreeing about Ken.

57
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,510
About Ken?

58
00:03:44,593 --> 00:03:45,423
What's going on?

59
00:03:45,506 --> 00:03:46,336
He's gone nuts.

60
00:03:46,419 --> 00:03:49,797
He wants to ask Ken to join us, even after
seeing the way he treated that Digimon.

61
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,337
Davis needs to realize that
people don't change that easily.

62
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:54,360
I'm not so sure Davis is wrong.

63
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:56,581
Maybe we're being too hard on it.

64
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:59,637
We have more important things
to worry about than Ken,

65
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,817
like why the control spires
started working again.

66
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,077
Yeah, like the spire that
was at Primary Village.

67
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,077
You're always first to
complete the test, Ken.

68
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,631
I'll be faster next time.

69
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:09,437
Look, I beat Ken on the math test.

70
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,977
Almost everyone beat him.

71
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:11,957
Look at the board.

72
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,057
Yeah, what happened?

73
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:14,797
He used to be tops on every subject.

74
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,877
Maybe his brain is
possessed by an evil alien.

75
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,857
I think your brain is possessed by a rock.

76
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:19,837
It's like he's given up.

77
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,237
They're right, I have given up.

78
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:22,577
I can't focus anymore.

79
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:24,037
I've got a lot on my mind.

80
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,160
No one understands. Ken! Huh?

81
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,270
Hey!

82
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,217
So what brings you all the way out here?

83
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,337
Did you come to remind me
that I've been a bad boy?

84
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,250
Come on, Ken.

85
00:04:35,333 --> 00:04:37,757
You've done some pretty rotten
things, but you're not an evil person.

86
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,700
I'm not? No.

87
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,937
The person that designed
the school's lunch menu?

88
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:42,549
Now that's an evil person.

89
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,595
That was a joke, Ken.

90
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:47,137
Sorry, I haven't been in
a laughing mood lately.

91
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:48,050
That's okay.

92
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:49,437
Look, I have an idea.

93
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:50,597
Why don't you come with me?

94
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,697
You can meet my friends
and tell them you're sorry.

95
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:53,610
But why?

96
00:04:53,693 --> 00:04:54,523
They hate me.

97
00:04:54,606 --> 00:04:55,436
They don't hate you, Ken.

98
00:04:55,519 --> 00:04:56,497
They just don't understand you.

99
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,757
I know you're sorry for what
you've done, but they don't.

100
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,117
What makes you so special?

101
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,377
I never said I was special.

102
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:03,497
I just think you're better than
you're giving yourself credit for.

103
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:04,440
I'm not sure.

104
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:07,037
Look, the digital world's
been pretty freaky lately.

105
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,179
We need your help.

106
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:10,957
After all, you're one of us Digidestined.

107
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:11,870
Huh?

108
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:13,490
Me?

109
00:05:13,573 --> 00:05:14,403
A Digidestined?

110
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:15,650
That's right.

111
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:17,209
Just one big happy family.

112
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,680
I don't know.

113
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:21,410
Thanks, Davis.

114
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:24,217
I appreciate you being honest
with me, but it just won't work.

115
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,700
I can't join you. What?

116
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:26,737
What do you mean?

117
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:27,650
I just can't.

118
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:28,563
Sorry.

119
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,571
Ken, where are you going?

120
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:31,817
Come on, Ken.

121
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:32,737
We could be your friends.

122
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:34,820
Please don't turn your back on us.

123
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:37,217
I really thought you were
getting through to him.

124
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,829
Why do you think he
didn't want to join us?

125
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:44,460
I think he just needs time, which
we don't have a whole lot of.

126
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:48,497
Hey, T .K., do you think
Davis is right about Ken?

127
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:50,757
Should we forgive him for what he's done?

128
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:54,137
I think everyone deserves a
second chance, Panama, even Ken.

129
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:56,037
I believe that he's
sorry for what he's done,

130
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:59,414
and it's time we forgive him
and let bygones be bygones.

131
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,508
I hope he forgives himself.

132
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:04,897
I've been thinking a lot about what
you said, and the answer is still no.

133
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:08,098
I'm sorry, Davis, but I
don't think it's a good idea.

134
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,125
Hey, Yoli, is something wrong?

135
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,390
Huh?

136
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,330
Let's see.

137
00:06:14,413 --> 00:06:16,417
I'll bet it's something to do with a boy.

138
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:18,220
Well, kind of. Let me guess.

139
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:22,117
This boy's been a real jerk in the past,
and you wonder if you should forgive him.

140
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,030
Yes, exactly.

141
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,297
Well, I think you should
give him another chance.

142
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:27,177
I mean, after all, he is your boyfriend.

143
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:28,320
Hmm? Oh, Yoli,

144
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,897
according to the latest
issue of Girly Girl magazine,

145
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:33,757
Your horoscope says you're going
to be lucky in love this month.

146
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:34,670
Wait a second.

147
00:06:34,753 --> 00:06:35,617
You guys have it all wrong.

148
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:36,657
I don't have a boyfriend.

149
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:37,860
Got it? Yep.

150
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,557
That's what they all say.

151
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:41,540
Ah, young love. Sweet.

152
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:44,330
Hmm.

153
00:06:44,413 --> 00:06:45,400
Now I'm really confused.

154
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,624
Maybe Davis is right about Ken.

155
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:51,817
If this is bothering you so much,
why don't you talk to Ken yourself?

156
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:53,317
It might make you feel better.

157
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,277
I know that's the right
thing to do, Poromon,

158
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:56,797
but I have this little
voice in my head that

159
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:58,737
keeps telling me Ken
is still untrustworthy.

160
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:00,060
It's up to you, Yoli,

161
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:04,278
but listening to little voices in
your head sounds pretty weird to me.

162
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:06,170
Rats!

163
00:07:06,253 --> 00:07:07,320
I don't know anymore.

164
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:10,382
I just hope I can make
the right decision, Poron.

165
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,680
Now, Sting Mom, go get him!

166
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,400
Twin Shaco!

167
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:19,884
Maybe if you've practiced more.

168
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:21,749
Spinning, spiking, strike.

169
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:26,557
Sting Mom, this insectoid Digimon bugs
opponents with his spiking strike attack.

170
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,757
Don't try bug spray on him, though.

171
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,369
It'll only make him angry.

172
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:36,320
He's gone to pieces you showed him Stingmon
oh can we not do that anymore today Ken

173
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:38,010
Unfortunately,

174
00:07:38,093 --> 00:07:39,757
I don't think that was the
last of the monsters will face

175
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:42,857
look at all these control spiders
I'm sorry I ever made them

176
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:45,837
something's going on and it
doesn't look good Maybe I should

177
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:49,802
join the other did she destined I
don't think we can do this alone

178
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:05,220
You have such white fur, your bubble blow
attack is almost as big as your appetites.

179
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:06,290
I'm glad.

180
00:08:06,373 --> 00:08:07,577
Next time we'll make s'mores.

181
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:08,490
How about that?

182
00:08:08,573 --> 00:08:10,177
I wonder where Palmon went to.

183
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:11,997
If she doesn't hurry back
with those marshmallows,

184
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:15,198
we're going to have to start
roasting some tree bark.

185
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:17,490
How pretty.

186
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,741
I bet Mimi will love this flower.

187
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,351
I should find more and make her a bouquet.

188
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:29,700
A human?

189
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,569
But what's she doing here?

190
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:34,537
I thought only children could
come to the digital world.

191
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:36,738
She doesn't look like a child to me.

192
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:40,020
And what's she doing
with that control spire?

193
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:44,440
Hair today, gone tomorrow.

194
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,480
Spirit needle!

195
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,068
Oh, this doesn't look good.

196
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,560
Go, flood the city.

197
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:57,630
Leave it in ruins.

198
00:08:57,713 --> 00:08:59,080
Now do as our command!

199
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,320
Oh, no!

200
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:02,750
Mimi!

201
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:03,663
Mimi, help!

202
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:05,700
Did you hear that?

203
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,380
Mimi, help!

204
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:09,717
You have to make me digivolve!

205
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,557
He's going to destroy the whole town!

206
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,117
Halmon, what are you talking about?

207
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:15,082
Who's going to destroy the town?

208
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,160
It's Golemon!

209
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:28,057
Golemon, a monstrous Digimon
made up of stone and minerals.

210
00:09:28,140 --> 00:09:30,964
His Crimson Curse attack
overpowers his enemies.

211
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:33,020
That was too close.

212
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:41,040
Are you okay?

213
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,680
I'm all right.

214
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:44,720
I just need to rest.

215
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,190
Go, Mimi.

216
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,842
Golemon's gonna destroy the dam.

217
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:52,720
Wait, stop.

218
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:54,077
Don't do anything.

219
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:54,990
Stop!

220
00:09:55,073 --> 00:09:56,895
The town is diviseless, you big bully!

221
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,700
There's no time.

222
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,078
You must warn them.

223
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:04,780
And I need to sleep.

224
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:06,960
Help on, hold on!

225
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,300
I can't do this alone.

226
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,160
I need help!

227
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:15,920
Somebody help me!

228
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,760
Gigi port, open!

229
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:28,580
Mimi, we're right here!

230
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:31,900
We came as fast as we could. Are you okay?

231
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:33,081
What's going on?

232
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,000
It's Golemon.

233
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:37,837
He's going to destroy the
dam and flood the city.

234
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:39,117
Why would he do that?

235
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,657
Did he just freak out or something?

236
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,269
We're running out of time!

237
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,477
Where's the tunnel?

238
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,917
At the end of the ravine,

239
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,237
all the Digimon down there will
be up to their digi-ears in water.

240
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,340
Hey, don't worry.

241
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:51,840
We're all over it.

242
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:54,794
Huh, let's take care of that rock head!

243
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,765
First we're gonna have
to get him off that dam!

244
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,260
It's my turn!

245
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:10,780
Thunder Blast!

246
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,360
Gold Rush!

247
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,920
Double Stars!

248
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:16,860
Great shot, guys!

249
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:19,410
Huh?

250
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,340
The shot didn't even freeze him.

251
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:25,800
He's too strong.

252
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:28,237
Look for his Dark Ring and destroy it.

253
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:29,280
I'm all over it.

254
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,680
I don't see a Dark Ring.

255
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,537
No Dark Ring, that means
he's not being controlled.

256
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:39,679
Yeah, just like that Thunder
Mon I fought last time.

257
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:46,880
Pegasus Mon.

258
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:51,700
That did it!

259
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:55,140
Crimson Feet!

260
00:11:57,860 --> 00:11:59,340
Hey, that's not fair!

261
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,280
My turn!

262
